column5:
Update News, add decomposition example

- Change compat for MOI
- Allow merge_strategy to be of type Union{Type{<: AbstractMergeStrategy}, OptionsFactory{<: AbstractMergeStrategy}}

Update REST for data used by frontend

This includes:
- Adding an endpoint for measurement compartment;
- Dropping the separate values endpoint, folding into measurements;
- Tweaking serializers to use more client-friendly naming;

With these changes in place, the custom queries that fetch *all* of a Study's
data for use in the frontend can get replaced with using the paged REST API
queries instead. Once the code is further adapted to use paged data, there
should be no more issues with "too much" data locking up the interface.

Adding integration test between EDD and ICE

Test is via the Experiment Description upload, and verifies:
+ that an EDD user may only see ICE parts if the corresponding ICE
  account has read permission on the part;
+ that EDD may reference ICE parts if visible, and create links to
  ICE parts;

Add support for more flexible input resolves

Extend the form for resolving input to EDD records, by allowing for:
- unmatched "locator" tokens to be created as new Lines;
- unmatched "type" tokens to be created as new provisional MeasurementTypes;
- option to toggle *all* unmatched "locator" tokens to new Lines;
- same for unmatched "type" tokens to new provisional MeasurementTypes;

Fix dev_lock.sh script

The script to refresh dependency versions was busted for two reasons:

1. The Docker image failed to build because its `$PATH` didn't contain the
   `poetry` binary;
2. Locking was set to not update dependencies;

These are now fixed.

Add correct syntax highlighting config to docs

As discovered in other projects, the default setup for code block syntax
highlighting in MkDocs uses `highlight.js`. This library presents a few
problems; it will:

- often guess languages wrong in short snippets;
- ignore metadata on language embedded in the docs;
- load a script from a third-party source;
- require scripting;

The config change here disables `highlight.js`, and instead loads a stylesheet
generated by `pygments`. This results in correct syntax highlighting, and makes
the highlighting entirely self-contained to the documentation image.

DOC: Lightly edited README

Cleaned up "tutorials" vs "examples";
Added reference to Canopy

Clarify what parameters are kwonly in documented signature of link_foo()

The documented signatures did not clearly show keyword-only parameters;
fix that.
